# Repo-root .gitignore for a UA-MIS capstone project.
#
# This file lands at the root of EVERY scaffolded repo and applies recursively,
# so it is the safety net for your first `git add -A` whichever starter you
# picked. Your starter ALSO ships its own .gitignore next to its code (in app/,
# or in frontend/ + backend/) with the rules specific to that stack.
#
# Why this matters: `node_modules/` is routinely hundreds of megabytes and a
# Rust `target/` is commonly 1-2 GB. GitHub hard-rejects any single file over
# 100 MB, and once big files are in git history the fix is a history rewrite,
# not a .gitignore edit. Prevention is five minutes; the cure is not.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED HERE: bin/, obj/ and vendor/. They are correct for
# .NET and Go, but a root-level rule applies to the whole tree, and the Rails
# starter commits bin/rails, bin/rake, bin/setup and vendor/.keep -- a root rule
# would silently drop them and leave a repo that cannot build. Those patterns
# live in the .NET and Go starters' own .gitignore instead, scoped to their
# component directory. Same reasoning for `.env.*`: the Laravel starter commits
# a real .env.testing, so only the genuinely-secret .env files are matched below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
target/
out/
.next/
.nuxt/
.output/
.svelte-kit/
.angular/
# Go's compiled test binary (`go test -c`)
*.test

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test / coverage output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local env and secrets -- NEVER commit these.
# Real secrets belong in Vault and arrive as an ExternalSecret; see
# .devops/secrets/README.md in this repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example
*.pem

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
